1 NOTE {geni:about_me} To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/54814315/kleng_maele-osmundson
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleng came to America in 1854, landing at Quebec, Canada, in June, going directly to La Salle county, Illinois where he remained about 6 years. He then moved to Fillmore county, Minnesota, staying about five years, and improving a
2 CONC  farm. He then sold out and in the spring of 1865 returned to Lee county, and located in Alto township. He held several local town offices, and was a republican politically. He had a farm of 280 acres, well cultivated and stocked.
2 CONC  - From the History of Lee County, published in 1881.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the founding members of the Norwegian Evangelical Lutheran Church (now Calvary Lutheran Church) Rural Lee, Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his wife, Caroline, and the five children in Illinois, Kleng took the remaining four children and moved to Hardin County, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: Øvre Mæle, Årdal, Rogaland, Norway
