1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burial record:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18799703/jacob-andrews-berglan
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob A. Berglan, 70, died at his home, three miles north of Amboy, Friday night at 8:55 o'clock following a three years illness, of complications.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Berglan was born in Auspion, Iowa, May 4, 1869, the son of Andrew and Wilhelmina Berglan. He was married at Araphoe, Okla., in 1908 to Flora A. Finnegan, who survives. He was a member of the Asbury Methodist church, west of Wa
2 CONC bash and had been a farmer his entire life. He moved from Wabash county to the Amboy community 11 years ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving besides the widow are one son, Harry, of Wabash; two stepsons, Walter and Roy Finnegan, both of Wabash, three brothers, Peter and George, of Norman, Okla., and Albert, of Henrietta, Okla. And four sisters, Mrs. Emma Grah
2 CONC am of Colony Okla., Mrs. Odessa Gibbs of Slick, Okla., Mrs. Sarah Hardesty of Cushing, Okla., and Mrs. May Chitwood of Tulsa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be conducted Tuesday morning at 10 o'clock at the Pleasant Grove Methodist church, north of Amboy and burial will be made in the Matlock cemetery, north of Wabash. The body will be removed from the Gene Lairy
2 CONC  funeral home in Amboy to the late residence Sunday morning, where friends may call.
2 CONT
