1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emma T. Anvick Emma T. Anvick died April 2, 1991, in Arcata at age 94. A native of Eureka, she was a resident of Arcata. Mrs. Anvick attended local schools including Jacoby Creek and Rolf Elementary schools and gra
2 CONC duated from Eureka High School and San Jose State University. She later taught at the Rolf Elementary School, Lincoln School, Warren Creek Elementary School and Jacoby Creek Elementary School. She was a charter member of the Baysi
2 CONC de Grange No. 500, and a member of the Bayside Garden Club and Bayside Community Church. She is survived by her son and his spouse, Theodore E. and Lenore Anvick of Arcata; a daughter and her spouse, Grace Ellen and Bill Greenwood
2 CONC  of Fair Oaks; a sister and her spouse, Oliva and Arne Simonsen; her grandchildren, Victor Anvick, Keith Anvick, Debbie Kearns, Teri Greenwood-Goodwin, Carol Greenwood-Cash, Tom Greenwood, Scott Anvick and Lynne Anvick; 10 great-g
2 CONC randchildren; and her nieces and nephews, Marjorie Adams, Eva Sandvig of Norway, Carla Abbett, Larry Torgersen, Mitch Torgersen, Carl Torgersen and Ole Per Tau of Norway. She is also survived by her sister-in-law, Mrs. Carl "Laura
2 CONC  Lea" Torgersen of Eureka. She was preceded in death by her husband, Clarence Anvick, in 1973; two brothers, Carl E. and Torger Torgersen; and a sister, Inga Logan. Friends are invited to attend funeral services Saturday, April 6,
2 CONC  1991, at 11 a.m. at Sanders Funeral Home Chapel, Eureka, with the Rev. Harold Jackson and the Rev. Dean Lindquist officiating. Interment will be at Ocean View Cemetery. Casketbearers will be Scott Anvick, Keith Anvick, Victor Anv
2 CONC ick, Don Wattenberger, Tom Torgersen and Calvin Kearns. Arrangements are under the direction of Sanders Funeral Home, where friends may visit today from noon until 5 p.m. and from 7 to 8:30 p.m. Memorial contributions may be made 
2 CONC to the Bayside Community Church, Old Arcata Road, Bayside 95524; or to Lifeline, 3800 Janes Road, Arcata 95521.
