1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000014232780166&
2 CONT
2 CONT Torgesen-Harper Spring Wedding Held Last Night
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the prettiest weddings of the season was celebrated last evening at the home of Mr. and Mrs. Harvey M. Harper, 1926 E street, when their daughter, Miss Laura Lea Harper, became the bride of Carl Torgeson, son of Mr. and Mrs
2 CONC . Ole Torgeson of the Peninsula.
2 CONT
2 CONT A bower of spring flowers and greenery had been erected at one end of the spacious living room of the home, and formed an attractive background for the charming bride and her attendants during the ceremony, which was performed by 
2 CONC Reverend George C. Pearson of the First Methodist church, Miss Verona Larson playing a wedding march. The bride in a lovely white gown and veil and carrying a bouquet of white carnations was attended by her sisters, Miss Ru-Flo Ha
2 CONC rper in green and silver, and Miss Marjorie Harper in rose and silver, as brides-maids, her sister, Mrs. Oscar Swanlund in blue and silver as matron of honor, and her youngest sister and brother, little Harmony and Harvey Harper, 
2 CONC dressed in white and carrying baskets of spring flowers. Harold Hilfiker supported the groom as best man. A number of close friends and relatives witnessed the ceremony and were afterwards entertained at dinner, the tables being .
2 CONC decorated in yellow carried out in daffodils and candles in this color. Mrs. Harper was assisted by Mrs. J, O. Baylor, Mrs. Fred Barnum, Mrs. E. R. Lindsay and Mrs.' W. L. Goyan, while Miss Lorene Barnum and Eleanor Perske assiste
2 CONC d in serving. The happy young couple left after dinner for San. Francisco, where a short honeymoon will be spent, and will return to make their home on the south jetty. Mrs. Torgerson is a popular member of the younger set here, h
2 CONC aving graduated from the Eureka high school and from the Western Normal of San Francisco, while her husband is a graduate of the local high school also, and ot Heald's business college in the bay city. Guests at the wedding last e
2 CONC vening in addition to members of the bridal party were the Misses Eleanor Jackson, Florence Swanlund, Emma Torgesen, Oliva Torgesen, Verona Larson, Inga Torgesen, Mr. and Mrs. Ole Torgesen, Mr. and Ms. A. Larsen, Mr. and Mrs.A. An
2 CONC vick, Mr. and Mrs. A. Knudsen, Mr. and Mrs. Elmer F. North, Mr. and Mrs. K. Anvick, Mrs. S. M. Ray, Messrs. Oscar Swanlund, Clarence Anvielt, Allen Anvick and Geddes Harper.
