1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1942 he was 5'8" tall, 145 pounds, was bald and had blue eyes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Obituary in The Daily Chronicle (9/27/1973)
2 CONT
2 CONT Owner and  operator of Bergie's Pheasant Tap in Sycamore, Illinois for over 35 years. Was rumored to have run a(n illicit) card game on the upper floor.
2 CONT
2 CONT One story: saved all the dimes from the till for many years and bought a new car with all dimes.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Salem Lutheran Church and the Sycamore Elks Lodge 1392. He was an avid sports fan and owned a home on Burch Island at Minaki, Ontario Canada.
