2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT Jasper Johnson Dies at His Home
2 CONT Morris Daily Herald Wednesday 08-22-1945
2 CONT
2 CONT Jasper S. Johnson, 52, a lifelong resident of Nettle Creek Township, died at 12:50 a.m. this morning in his home after several months illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT His body was taken to the Hoganson funeral home and will remain until Friday afternoon when it will be returned to his own home to remain for services there Saturday afternoon at 1:30 and at 2:30 in Stavanger Lutheran Church. The 
2 CONC Rev. Harold Rye will officiate and burial will be in Stavanger cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Johnson was born on a farm in Nettle Creek Township, Oct. 7, 1892, and died on the farm where he was born. He was married Oct. 3, 1913, to Lillian Wicks.
2 CONT
2 CONT The widow survives him with two daughters, Mrs. Selmar Lysland of Paw Paw and Mrs. Vernon Anderson of Aurora; two grandchildren; five brothers, Oscar of Iowa, Silas of Nettle Creek Township, Milton of Milwaukee, Wis., Irwin of Mor
2 CONC ris, and Stanley of Newark; and a sister, Mrs. Joseph Voga of Sandwich. His aged mother, Mrs. Melinda Johnson, resides at the corner of Vino Street and Fremont Avenue.
