1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lauritz came to Fillmore County, MN in 1883, where he worked for three years before coming to North Dakota in 1886.
2 CONT Unfamiliar with the English language, he worked for a Norwegian farmer until he began farming in Farmington Township. 
2 CONT Emma and Lauritz farmed there for several years before they purchased land in Martin Township on November 16, 1897.
2 CONT They were members of the Landstad Lutheran Church, Auburn, ND, and celebrated their Golden Wedding Anniversary there in 1939.  He served as its secretary for 34 years, and was a member of the District School Board.  They had nine 
2 CONC children.  Stories were obtained from "Walsh Heritage", published by the Walsh County Historical Society in 1978.
2 CONT
2 CONT
